Subject: [PATCH 1/3] app: every file.save says why - reason "user" or "auto"
From: Office Kit
Date: 2026-10-18
Upstream: https://github.com/BRF-Tech/filex-office-editor (AGPL-3.0-or-later, Copyright (C) 2026 BRF Tech)
Base: v0.3.1 57dda3dae99af78eb26b3c64b69f1e3f711f0757 (the tag commit; the next main commit acc87f88da47 changes only README.md)
Apply: git -C <filex checkout> apply <this file>   (in order: 0001, 0002, 0003)
Modified: this patch changes filex-office-editor; see docs/office-editor-patches.md (Office Kit)

Office Kit: file.save에 reason을 더한다 ("user" = 사용자 저장, "auto" = 10분 자동 저장). 자동 저장 중 누른 저장은 그 뒤에 따로 한다.

file.save carries `reason`: "user" for a save the person asked for (the
editor's Save or Ctrl+S, filex's Save / the host's {hid, request:'save'},
a switch of view, the last writer leaving), "auto" for the ten-minute save.
filex writes both as a new version, as before; a host that keeps an
autosave apart from the file (a recovery copy) tells them apart by it.
Alone, the save goes through the SDK's raw request (the 0.53 SDK's save()
has no field for it); together, coedit-client passes it with `through`.

Saves stay one at a time (src/app/save-queue.ts), but a Save pressed
during an autosave is made after it instead of being answered by it.

